{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tied-type type is used as an attribute of the tied element to specify where the visual representation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a tie begins and ends. A tied element which joins two notes of the same pitch can be specified with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tied-type start on the first note and tied-type stop on the second note. To indicate a note should be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"undamped, use a single tied element with tied-type let-ring. For other ties that are visually attached to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single note, such as a tie leading into or out of a repeated section or coda, use two tied elements on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same note, one start and one stop."}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/continue","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/letRing","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/start","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/stop"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum\/Equatable-Implementations"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltied\/kind-swift.enum"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/Kind-swift.enum","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In start-stop cases, ties can add more elements using a continue type. This is typically used to specify the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"formatting of cross-system ties.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When multiple elements with the same tag are used within the same note, their order within the MusicXML","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document should match the musical score order. For example, a note with a tie at the end of a first ending","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"should have the tied element with a type of start precede the tied element with a type of stop.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Enumeration","symbolKind":"enum","title":"MXLTied.Kind","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLTiedV4KindO","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"extendedModule":"IvorMXL"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/s9EscapableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Escapable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTied/Kind-swift.enum":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tied-type type is used as an attribute of the tied element to specify where the visual representation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"ty